<.shell title="View switch" current={:view_switch}>
  <h1>View switch</h1>
  <p class="lead">Switches a list between a few views, with counts.</p>

  <div class="demo">
    <.filter_bar
      for={sample_filters()}
      id="view-switch-demo"
      count="131 members"
      onsubmit="return false"
    >
      <:lead>
        <.view_switch label="Awards">
          <:view patch="#" current={true} count={131}>Active</:view>
          <:view patch="#" count={40}>Expired</:view>
        </.view_switch>
      </:lead>
      <:search field={sample_filters()[:q]} />
    </.filter_bar>
  </div>

  <h3>On its own</h3>
  <div class="demo">
    <.view_switch label="Year">
      <:view patch="#" current={true}>2026</:view>
      <:view patch="#">2025</:view>
      <:view patch="#">2024</:view>
    </.view_switch>
  </div>

  <h2>When to use</h2>
  <p>
    A list of a few dozen to a few hundred rows that splits one obvious way, such as a qualification's active and expired awards. Put it first in a
    <a href={page_path(:filter_bar)}>filter bar</a>
    with a search box, or on its own for a few years.
  </p>

  <h2>When not to use</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>More than about 5 views. Use a menu in a filter bar.</li>
    <li>Pages about one record. Use <a href={page_path(:tabs)}>tabs</a>.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How it works</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Each view is a link that patches the page, so the URL says which view is showing.</li>
    <li>
      The current view is filled. The count says how many rows each view has before the search.
    </li>
    <li>A search box beside it searches the view that is showing.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>In the app</h2>
  <p>
    <code>&lt;.view_switch label="…"&gt;</code>
    with a <code>:view</code>
    slot per view, each with its <code>patch</code>, <code>current</code>, and <code>count</code>.
  </p>
</.shell>
